+
+This instance has {inst['n_vertices']} vertices, numbered 0 through {inst['n_vertices'] - 1}.  It is the full subdivision of a {inst['core_degree']}-regular graph.  The core vertices are:
+  {core}
+
+Every other vertex has degree two.  The complete edge set is encoded by the following subdivision table.  A row "s: x y" means that edges s-x and s-y exist.  There are no other edges.
+{rows}
+
+Your certificate must be a sorted triple [s1,s2,s3] of distinct degree-two vertices.  Deleting these three vertices must leave exactly two connected components, each of exactly {inst['required_side_size']} vertices.  Each deleted vertex must have one neighbor in each component.  The two components are then the branch sets of U and V, and the three singleton deleted vertices are the branch sets of A, B, and C.  Component order and the assignment of the three singletons to A,B,C do not matter.  Vertex identifiers are integers; indexing is zero-based.
