I found one design issue during audit: the compressed three-vertex answer was valid, but it made the paper’s branch-set object less visible than necessary. I’m tightening the family before finalizing it: the solver will now return the complete five branch sets (a true spanning induced-minor model), while the planted separator remains the construction certificate. This keeps the answer under the cap, makes verification exactly the paper’s definition, and enlarges the structure-aware answer space without inflating the hidden witness.
