codex
Implemented a deterministic, self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s native induced-minor branch-set definition.

Key results:

- All local G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- 0/200,000 structure-aware random candidates verified.
- Five adversarial attacks scored 0/8 each.
- Exact Stoer–Wagner reference algorithm solved 8/8, as expected for Track B.
- Shipping answer: 425 characters, 105 atoms.
- Intended route: 192 operations; reference median: 6,700 operations.
- Canonical key passed 60 relabelling checks and distinguished 20/20 seeds.

Files:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.08332/gen_2402_08332.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.08332/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.08332/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.08332/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.08332/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.08332/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The result is parked rather than rejected or claimed fully hardened. Every required oracle call returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” so there were zero valid STEP 4 or G9 oracle attempts. The error transcripts are preserved honestly; rerunning the three oracle arms after restoring quota is the only remaining work. This does not indicate a G, H, or V failure.

Source: [arXiv:2402.08332](https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.08332).
